.TH "ARC-EXPLAIN" "1" "2026-09-27" "arc-cli" "Arc Manual"
.SH "NAME"
arc\-explain \- explain an execution plan without mutating data
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
arc explain [\-\-json] COMMAND ...
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Plan an Arc operation through its real dry\-run path and show the decisions and native stages without mutating archives, destinations, transaction state, or remote content.
.SH "OPTIONS"
\-\-json
.SH "SEMANTICS"
Explain forces the nested operation into dry\-run mode. The plan records format/backend selection, typed verification\-policy negotiation, publication policy, locality/staging decisions, and source\-removal policy where applicable. It is diagnostic evidence, not a promise that external state will remain unchanged between planning and execution.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
arc explain convert a.zip \-tzst
.PP
arc explain \-\-json create backup.tar src/
.SH "SEE ALSO"
arc\-convert(1), arc\-recover(1), arc\-backends(7)
